Problem Statement : Write a Python program to check that a string contains only a certain set of characters (in this case a-z, A-Z and 0-9).

# Import regular expression module

import re
s = input("Enter a string :")
if re.match("[a-zA-Z0-9]+",s) is not None: 
    print("String contains only letters and numbers.")
else:
    print("String contains invalid characters:")
